{
  "$comment": "🔴 TUYA'S OWN Wi-Fi Lock Pro DP MAP — the platform standard, NOT a vendor's. Source: https://developer.tuya.com/en/docs/iot/wifi-dp?id=K9fewhnlvk6by\n\nSTANDALONE, and that is the whole point. DP numbers are assigned PER PRODUCT CATEGORY at PID creation, so there is no shared catalogue that can serve both this and a vendor map. Proof: DP 76 is `fill_light` here and `unlock_ble` on Luona's DS013-T3 — the same number turns on a lamp or opens a door. DP 16 is `duress_alarm` here and `bulk_password_add` there. Selecting from one catalogue would have meant one of them was silently wrong.\n\nUse this as the reference map for a lock built to Tuya's standard. Do NOT use it as a fallback for an unidentified lock — an unknown lock may be a Residential Lock, where DP 16 is `sound level of the chime`.",
